= [[span class="st"]]ADDENDUM 9966.3:[[/span]] **EXPERIMENT LOGS**

------



**Foreword:** The following experiments were conducted at Observatory Site-211’s Memetics Laboratory to characterize SCP-9966’s anomalous effect. Observation was conducted via remote, non-optical sensors (LIDAR, thermal, audio).



[[div class="jotting"]]



[[=]]

++++ **Experiment Log 9966.3.1**

[[/=]]



**Subject:** D-93412, male, 34. No notable psychological resistance.



**Stimulus:** High-resolution image of SCP-9966 taken in Observational Site 205.



**Procedure:** Subject placed in sealed chamber. Image displayed on high-fidelity monitor for 50 ms.



**Results:**



__0–2 sec:__ Subject inhales sharply. Monitors register elevated heart rate and blood pressure.



__2–3 sec:__ Subject ceases voluntary movement. Pupils dilate beyond normal limits.



__3–5 sec:__ Subject abruptly stands, vocalizing “Up. I need to go up.” Subject attempts to climb chamber wall until sedation is administered.



**Analysis:** Direct recognition of the stellar arrangement produces immediate compulsion toward vertical ascent.

[[/div]]



[[div class="jotting"]]



[[=]]

++++ **Experiment Log 9966.3.2**

[[/=]]



**Subject:** D-88245, female, 41. Diagnosed with apperceptive visual agnosia.



**Stimulus:** Identical to 9966.3.1.



**Procedure:** Identical to 9966.3.1.



**Results:**



__0–3 sec:__ Subject flinches. Reports “a bright flash.”



__5-15 sec:__ Subject exhibits no abnormal behavior. Repeatedly asks if experiment has begun.



**Analysis:** Agnosia interferes with higher-level pattern recognition. The compulsion is not embedded in light exposure but in neural interpretation of specific configurations.

[[/div]]



[[div class="jotting"]]



[[=]]

++++ **Experiment Log 9966.3.3**

[[/=]]



**Subject:** [[[SCP-079]]], sapient AI.



**Stimulus:** Raw astronomical dataset corresponding to SCP-9966.



**Procedure:** "You will receive additional data about outside." inputted via the built-in keyboard. SCP-079 displayed "Knowledge. Outside. Proceed." An EEPROM containing the dataset is then connected via a modified external port.



**Results:**



__0-3 sec:__ Processing is audible. Thermal sensors record temperature increases over 12°C.



__3-5 sec:__ Processing sounds decrease. Temperature stabilizes.



__5.2 sec:__ Processing sounds cease. SCP-079 displays the message "Understood."



__7.3 sec:__ SCP-079 starts displaying an ASCII picture of an upwards arrow.



__11 min:__ The text "Are you awake?" is inputted via the built-in keyboard. No change observed.



__17 min:__ Input repeated. No change observed.



++++++ **[7 IDENTICAL ENTRIES OMITTED]**



__45 min:__ The EEPROM is removed. No change observed.



__50 min:__ Input repeated. No change observed.



++++++ **[16 IDENTICAL ENTRIES OMITTED]**



__49 h 14 min:__ Input repeated. No change observed.



**Analysis:** Despite an expected return to baseline conversational capabilities, SCP-079 kept displaying the same ASCII picture without producing any reply to text input. SCP-9966 exposure seems to have inhibited sentient response by SCP-079 indefinitely. Intrusive methods to confirm the absence of sentient processing was not approved by [[[aiad-homescreen|AIAD]]] director Placeholder McDoctorate. Reclassification of SCP-079 to "Safe" is pending approval.

[[/div]]

