= [[span class="st"]]**ADDENDUM 9966.8:**[[/span]] **INCIDENT LOG 9966-Ω**

------

**Foreword:** On 2034/07/05, routine containment verification of SCP-9966 was scheduled under standard containment protocols. The event marked the first recorded deviation from SCP-9966’s previously observed compulsive “ascension” behavior. Subsequent analysis confirmed a shift in anomalous effect parameters, now presenting as a directly lethal cognitohazard. The following is a consolidated timeline.



[[div class="notation"]]

__0.0 sec:__ Observation Dome light saturation grid intentionally disabled for calibration. Dome shutters retract, providing full visibility of SCP-9966.



__0.7 sec:__ All exposed individuals simultaneously inhale sharply. Cardiac activity spikes noted.



__1.4 sec:__ Universal pupillary dilation observed. Subjects enter catatonic state. No voluntary movement.



__2.8 sec:__ EEG activity collapses across all subjects.[[span class="fnnum2"]].[[/span]][[span class="fncon2"]]Electroencephalographic measurement devices were implanted to all personnel stationed in Observatory Sites 200-213.[[/span]]



__3.1 sec:__ Brainstem reflexes cease. Subjects no longer respirating.



__4.0 sec:__ All 14 individuals clinically deceased.



__6.0 sec:__ Automated emergency floodlights reengage. Medical response deployed. No resuscitation successful.



[[/div]]

**Exposed Personnel:** 9 researchers, 3 technicians, and 2 armed security staff.



**Casualties:** 14 (100% mortality among exposed personnel)



**Analysis:** Necropsy of subjects reveals total cessation of higher brain activity consistent with instantaneous cortical failure. No evidence of attempted motor ascent or compulsive behavior previously associated with SCP-9966 exposure.

