On 2036/02/09 RAISA operatives recovered the following document, bearing the verified signatures of all standing Ethics Committee members. Within twenty-four hours of recovery, all communication channels with the Committee and with MTF Omega-1 (“Law’s Left Hand”) failed without explanation. No further contact has been established.



[[div class="darkdocument"]]

Committee Chair ████████████:



The Committee was established to [DATA EXPUNGED].



We acknowledge that Protocol-NOCTIS achieved its operational objective. ████████████. Survival was purchased. ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████.



We did not protect. We mutilated.



████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████.



Protection ended when vision ended. ████████████ containment. ███████████████ Foundation survival only.



If survival requires the erasure of what it is to be human, then what has survived?

------

= [42 consecutive pages redacted in full.]

------

Final Statement:

The Ethics Committee is hereby dissolved.



History may decide if we were necessary. ████████████████████████.

[[/div]]



With the dissolution of the Ethics Committee and the disappearance of MTF Omega-1, all oversight mechanisms external to the O5 Council have effectively ceased. No replacement structures have been authorized.



Protocol-NOCTIS remains in operational readiness, its continuation and potential execution entrusted solely to the judgment of the Council.



For archival purposes, this entry is designated the final Ethics Committee record. All subsequent policy regarding SCP-9966 shall be considered outside of ethical review.

