The following are communication transcripts, research notes, samples and findings from Project Devil's Nine Questions.



[[div class="blockquote"]]

**Site-898 Exterior Lot CCTV**

**Date:** 04/03/1975

**Personnel Present:** Dr. Hellen Gibbs, Dr. Fate Hargroves, Dr. Atticus Rune

------



//Dr. Gibbs' van is painted black, caked in mud, dust and is covered in countless dents and scratches. Two novelty bumper stickers read "I BRAKE FOR OUTCROPS" and "GEOLOGISTS NEVER TAKE SCHIST FOR GRANITE". It is worn, but well-used and far-traveled.// 



//Dr. Gibbs hoists open the trunk with a grunt. Drs. Rune and Hargroves approach, both carrying duffle bags.//



**Dr. Rune**: We sure this puppy is gonna make it all the way down the coast? 



//Dr. Hargroves gives a small chuckle.//



**Dr. Gibbs:** Likely. //[She pats the trunk door]// If it doesn’t? There’s a spare tire and a toolbox in the trunk. 



**Dr. Rune:** Hope you’re right. 



//Dr. Rune shoves his hands into his pockets.//



**Dr. Rune:** By the by, how long you think we’ll be in each state? On average. 



//Dr. Gibbs begins to load the trunk, and pauses briefly to think.//



**Dr. Gibbs:** Probably a day or so -- not counting travel, that is. It will likely depend on what we find and the weather. 



**Dr. Hargroves:** I see a tent in there, are we roughing it completely?



**Dr. Gibbs:** For the most part, yes. [[footnote]] Request for a camper was left unanswered by Foundation Human Resources. Dr. Gibbs later stated: “A camper probably wouldn’t have made it five minutes on the roads we were taking, anyways.”[[/footnote]] Being easily mobile will make things more efficient. //[Dr. Gibbs grimaces.]// Primarily because I don't want to work out the logistics of places to stay. 



**Dr. Hargroves:** Wonderful! 



**Dr. Rune:** Well, hell, that blows some of my ideas outta the water. We’ll make it work, somehow. You’d just better hope that the weather doesn’t fuck us sideways.



**Dr. Hargroves:** We will be making pit stops, mm?



**Dr. Gibbs:** Mostly for food.



//Dr. Hargroves bumps Dr. Rune with her hip.//



**Dr. Hargroves:** Then it seems your idea is still a go! We can hit some diners or bars.



//Dr. Rune playfully nudges her shoulder in return, chuckling.//



**Dr. Rune:** Oh, good, maybe this won't be a shit show, then. Bars and diners is what I was thinking, but camping knocks out motels. Those are some of the best places to get locals talking. Can't believe I’m bein' paid to drink and get people loose-lipped on the job. 



//Dr. Gibbs cracks a small smile.//



**Dr. Gibbs:** What phrasing do I put on the paper to justify using the research grant for //that// sort of expense?



