__**Sample Name:**__ Sandstone, Kanawha Formation



__**Sample Observations:**__

Sample is a lithic sandstone.[[footnote]] "Lithic" refers to eroded fragments that now form grains in a sedimentary rock. [[/footnote]] It's a primarily clay matrix intermixed with grains of feldspar and quartz.



__**Akiva Reaction:**__ 

While not noticeable within the sample itself, or broken off pieces, it was found during collection that especially large deposits of sandstones seem to "whisper" when strong winds blow through them, but the wind typically renders the speech unintelligible.



------



__**Sample Name:**__ Coal, New River Formation



__**Sample Observations:**__

Sample of bituminous coal with a dark brown-black coloration, discovered within a Carboniferous age sandstone.  



__**Akiva Reaction:**__ 

During the night, knocking on the sample occasionally produces a response knock from within. 



------



__**Sample Name:**__ Unconsolidated sand, Quaternary Alluvium deposit 



__**Sample Observations:**__

Loose quartz sand and gravel that has been deposited by either running water, flood plains, or lake beaches. The specific sample gathered was taken from a stream bed. 



__**Akiva Reaction:**__ 

Sample resonates in response to human whistling, amplifying its volume and carry distance significantly. However, it appears that the resulting whistling induced the attention of [https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-6448 hostile cervine anomalies] that were, unbeknownst to the team, nearby. Further testing aborted.



------



__**Sample Name:**__ Shale, Bluefield Formation



__**Sample Observations:**__

Terrestrially deposited shale comprised of various clays and plagioclase. The rock is a deep red in coloration due to the presence of oxidized hematite. 



__**Akiva Reaction:**__ 

It is believed that the iron content within the sample was capable of partially fending off the presence of the previously mentioned entities, due to the dropping of the sample seeming to dissuade the anomalies from approaching the team's nearby hiding place.



